{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M6tXADK21bu4RhDppGSuKK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment score scale 1 2 3 4 5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ACLRollingReview (@ReviewAcl) / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/reviewacl\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/acl-rolling-review\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review scoring system:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the specific details about the exact 1-5 scale definitions for the overall assessment score in the 2025-2026 review form. The search found references to the review form page (aclrollingreview.org/reviewform), but the detailed content wasn't captured in the results.\n\nOne forum post mentioned that Overall Assessment (OA) descriptions include a 5.0 \"Award-worthy (top 2.5%)\" level, but the complete scale definitions for all score levels (1-5) aren't fully detailed in these results.\n\nFor the complete and official score scale definitions, you may need to visit the ACL Rolling Review website directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines to access the full review guidelines and scoring rubric.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16acc6c0-2bc8-4647-8b19-962cbe1441c4","uuid":"c0dba2b6-3732-4877-8f6a-a8832ac4a6b1","timestamp":"2026-05-16T17:16:42.462Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment score scale 1 2 3 4 5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Egja3MhUma7va6xnpa5hCN","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"ACLRollingReview (@ReviewAcl) / X","url":"https://x.com/reviewacl"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/acl-rolling-review"}]},"Based on the web search results, I found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review scoring system:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the specific details about the exact 1-5 scale definitions for the overall assessment score in the 2025-2026 review form. The search found references to the review form page (aclrollingreview.org/reviewform), but the detailed content wasn't captured in the results.\n\nOne forum post mentioned that Overall Assessment (OA) descriptions include a 5.0 \"Award-worthy (top 2.5%)\" level, but the complete scale definitions for all score levels (1-5) aren't fully detailed in these results.\n\nFor the complete and official score scale definitions, you may need to visit the ACL Rolling Review website directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines to access the full review guidelines and scoring rubric."],"durationSeconds":5.596883703000003}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XvZAekFdTAKsqtbbWWzhTQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ARR ACL Rolling Review reviewer form dimensions soundness novelty significance clarity 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here is information about the ARR ACL Rolling Review reviewer form dimensions:\n\n## Review Form Dimensions\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness\nSoundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\nGiven the paper length, reviewers should assess whether it is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and consider the depth and/or breadth of research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\n### Excitement and Overall Assessment\nThe overall assessment score is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n### Clarity and Other Considerations\nReviewers should identify concerns that would cause prioritizing other high-quality papers, which could include concerns about correctness of results or argumentation, limited perceived impact of methods or findings, lack of clarity in exposition, or any other reason why interested readers may gain less from this paper than from others under consideration.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16acc6c0-2bc8-4647-8b19-962cbe1441c4","uuid":"8f4a8713-0f07-47ed-ad20-b322442bc902","timestamp":"2026-05-16T17:16:44.557Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ARR ACL Rolling Review reviewer form dimensions soundness novelty significance clarity 2025","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VVCb9bGcHfGv9rBbSTGXK2","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ARR Changelog – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"}]},"Based on the search results, here is information about the ARR ACL Rolling Review reviewer form dimensions:\n\n## Review Form Dimensions\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness\nSoundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\nGiven the paper length, reviewers should assess whether it is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and consider the depth and/or breadth of research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\n### Excitement and Overall Assessment\nThe overall assessment score is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n### Clarity and Other Considerations\nReviewers should identify concerns that would cause prioritizing other high-quality papers, which could include concerns about correctness of results or argumentation, limited perceived impact of methods or findings, lack of clarity in exposition, or any other reason why interested readers may gain less from this paper than from others under consideration."],"durationSeconds":7.047666509000003}}
