{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0193HtEU5yU42coqYyW4NAE4","type":"tool_result","content":"# ACL Rolling Review Scoring Rubrics\n\n## Overall Assessment\nScale: 1-5 (with half-point increments)\n- **5**: \"Consider for Award: I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award\"\n- **4.5**: Borderline Award\n- **4**: \"Conference: I think this paper could be accepted to an *ACL conference\"\n- **3.5**: Borderline Conference\n- **3**: \"Findings: I think this paper could be accepted to the Findings of the ACL\"\n- **2.5**: Borderline Findings\n- **2**: Substantial revisions needed by next cycle\n- **1.5**: Substantial revisions requiring extended timeline\n- **1**: Not suitable for resubmission or ACL community\n\n## Soundness\nScale: 1-5 (with half-point increments)\n- **5**: \"Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen\"\n- **4**: \"Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims\"\n- **3**: \"Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims\"\n- **2**: \"Poor: Some of the main claims are not sufficiently supported\"\n- **1**: \"Major Issues: This study is not yet sufficiently thorough to warrant publication\"\n\n## Excitement/Novelty\nScale: 1-5 (with half-point increments)\n- **5**: \"Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation\"\n- **4**: \"Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend\"\n- **3**: \"Interesting: I might mention some points of this paper to others\"\n- **2**: \"Potentially Interesting: does not resonate with me, but it might with others\"\n- **1**: \"Not Exciting: does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others\"\n\n## Reviewer Confidence\nScale: 1-5\n- **5**: \"Positive that my evaluation is correct. I read the paper very carefully\"\n- **4**: \"Quite sure. I tried to check the important points carefully\"\n- **3**: \"Pretty sure, but there's a chance I missed something\"\n- **2**: \"Willing to defend my evaluation, but it is fairly likely that I missed some details\"\n- **1**: \"Not my area, or paper is very hard to understand. My evaluation is just an educated guess\"\n\n## Reproducibility\nScale: 1-5\n- **5**: Could easily reproduce results\n- **4**: Could mostly reproduce with minor variations\n- **3**: Could reproduce with some difficulty; underspecified parameters\n- **2**: Hard to reproduce; unavailable data or insufficient details\n- **1**: Cannot reproduce results\n\n## Datasets & Software\nScale: 1-5 (same for both)\n- **5**: Enabling—should affect research project selection\n- **4**: Useful—recommended for ongoing work\n- **3**: Potentially useful—might help some researchers\n- **2**: Documentary—useful for replication only\n- **1**: No usable resources submitted\n\n## Author Identity Knowledge\nScale: 1-5\n- **5**: Identity known from double-blind violations\n- **4**: Known from preprints or workshop papers\n- **3**: Identifiable from submission contents\n- **2**: Known from social media or informal communication\n- **1**: No educated guess about identity"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16acc6c0-2bc8-4647-8b19-962cbe1441c4","uuid":"a126103f-a18c-42f8-aa35-030660eb0eed","timestamp":"2026-05-16T17:17:05.203Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":25365,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# ACL Rolling Review Scoring Rubrics\n\n## Overall Assessment\nScale: 1-5 (with half-point increments)\n- **5**: \"Consider for Award: I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award\"\n- **4.5**: Borderline Award\n- **4**: \"Conference: I think this paper could be accepted to an *ACL conference\"\n- **3.5**: Borderline Conference\n- **3**: \"Findings: I think this paper could be accepted to the Findings of the ACL\"\n- **2.5**: Borderline Findings\n- **2**: Substantial revisions needed by next cycle\n- **1.5**: Substantial revisions requiring extended timeline\n- **1**: Not suitable for resubmission or ACL community\n\n## Soundness\nScale: 1-5 (with half-point increments)\n- **5**: \"Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen\"\n- **4**: \"Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims\"\n- **3**: \"Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims\"\n- **2**: \"Poor: Some of the main claims are not sufficiently supported\"\n- **1**: \"Major Issues: This study is not yet sufficiently thorough to warrant publication\"\n\n## Excitement/Novelty\nScale: 1-5 (with half-point increments)\n- **5**: \"Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation\"\n- **4**: \"Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend\"\n- **3**: \"Interesting: I might mention some points of this paper to others\"\n- **2**: \"Potentially Interesting: does not resonate with me, but it might with others\"\n- **1**: \"Not Exciting: does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others\"\n\n## Reviewer Confidence\nScale: 1-5\n- **5**: \"Positive that my evaluation is correct. I read the paper very carefully\"\n- **4**: \"Quite sure. I tried to check the important points carefully\"\n- **3**: \"Pretty sure, but there's a chance I missed something\"\n- **2**: \"Willing to defend my evaluation, but it is fairly likely that I missed some details\"\n- **1**: \"Not my area, or paper is very hard to understand. My evaluation is just an educated guess\"\n\n## Reproducibility\nScale: 1-5\n- **5**: Could easily reproduce results\n- **4**: Could mostly reproduce with minor variations\n- **3**: Could reproduce with some difficulty; underspecified parameters\n- **2**: Hard to reproduce; unavailable data or insufficient details\n- **1**: Cannot reproduce results\n\n## Datasets & Software\nScale: 1-5 (same for both)\n- **5**: Enabling—should affect research project selection\n- **4**: Useful—recommended for ongoing work\n- **3**: Potentially useful—might help some researchers\n- **2**: Documentary—useful for replication only\n- **1**: No usable resources submitted\n\n## Author Identity Knowledge\nScale: 1-5\n- **5**: Identity known from double-blind violations\n- **4**: Known from preprints or workshop papers\n- **3**: Identifiable from submission contents\n- **2**: Known from social media or informal communication\n- **1**: No educated guess about identity","durationMs":9662,"url":"https://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"}}
